Q: Convert a 2d array to an associative array by parsing one column as the key path and another column as the value A: <p>So not use <code>eval()</code> in code if there is any other way; and their usually is. Parse the name values and manually construct the desired keys path from the matched parts. <a href="https://3v4l.org/dF4dj#v" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$result = [];
foreach ($datas as ['name' =&gt; $n, 'value' =&gt; $v]) {
    if (preg_match('/(.*)\[(\d+)]/', $n, $m)) {
        $result[$m[1]][$m[2]] = $v;
    } else {
        $result[$n] = $v;
    }
}
var_export($result);
</code></pre>
<p>Or with sscanf(): <a href="https://3v4l.org/8VQH7#v" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$result = [];
foreach ($datas as ['name' =&gt; $n, 'value' =&gt; $v]) {
    if (sscanf($n, '%[^[][%d', $k1, $k2) === 2) {
        $result[$k1][$k2] = $v;
    } else {
        $result[$n] = $v;
    }
}
var_export($result);
</code></pre>
<p>Both scripts above deliver this output:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>array (
  'scattr' =&gt; '250',
  'scattrtel' =&gt; '9830293789',
  'scattrcolor' =&gt; '#2764C6',
  'scattrta' =&gt; '',
  'scattrcb' =&gt; '',
  'scattrmcb' =&gt; 
  array (
    1 =&gt; '10',
    4 =&gt; '40',
  ),
  'scattrmrdo' =&gt; '20',
  'scattrselect' =&gt; '30',
  'pwpus-shortcode-nonce' =&gt; '028c9426c5',
  '_wp_http_referer' =&gt; '/wp-admin/admin-ajax.php',
)
</code></pre>
